Z||000010||sqoach||01-05-2001||01:38 AM||||sweetness!<BR>pretty cool with the tweeter in the thingamagiggy.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>i couldn't ever figure out a spot to mount tweeters, so i got some 4x6s with the swiveling tweeter. aim it right at my head. sounds awesome.<BR>well you got the mids and highs, how 'bout the lows?<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG"> ||||reg||14
Z||000011||Oreif||01-05-2001||02:37 AM||||Cheever2 ~ I'll take pics of the interior when I get the woofers installed where the 4X6 use to go so everyone can see how I mounted them. (there will be no panels   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  )<P>mOpe ~ When you get a Fiero just let me know and we can discuss options and how much you want to spend. (I use to install stereo systems as a side job for many years)<P>William ~ Due to the height of the tweeter, I had to cut out the center plastic "grill". As for recovering them, I just took a razor and cut the very bottom edge of the cloth. Then I super glued one edge to the new cloth (available at radio shack) let it dry good, then stretched it taunt and glued iy on the other side. Once dry I did the same to the ends. Also acoustically it is better to remove the plastic. Especially if you have a tweeter (seperate or part of a coaxial 4X10)<P>sqoach ~ As for sub, I'll be making a mount to hold an 8" Rockford Fosgate under the dash (in place of the stock sub) powered with a 200W sub amp. The rest of the system will be powered by a 50WX4 amp. I will also have electronic crossovers and a digital surround sound processor with spacial seperation to control it all.<P>It won't be a super loud "Booming" system but it will be very clean sounding with excellent tonal quality with distinctive octive resolution.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Oreif||01-05-2001||02:56 PM||||BTW ~ The paint used to match the tweeters to the panel is called "Gunship Gray"<BR>Federal Stock # FS36118 incase anyone wants to paint other interior items for the dark gray years.||||reg||3
