Z||000014||Oreif||01-05-2001||08:27 PM||||I bought the sets for $169.00 each. I got them from an on-line car stereo place. I'll post the link later (at work now) They are the 4" EX II series. (Crutchfield had them at $229 a set).<BR>I don't mind people copying my idea's as long as they send all earned profits to me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  (j/k)||||reg||1
Z||000015||Monkeyman||01-05-2001||09:53 PM||||I have a set of JBL 5 1/4" separates.  The mids will rest in the stock front speaker locations (with 1/2" spacers, they'll even let me use the stock speaker covers).  The tweeters will go in a custom dash panel (to replace the cover over the stereo/HVAC--black Lexan to match the face of my stereo) where the vents are now.  I'll cover the vent hole (in the dash).  I've kept the center vents closed for about a week just to see if it would get too cold without them.  No problems so far.||||reg||1
Z||000016||DXR_DAD||01-05-2001||10:28 PM||||Nice job Oreif!!<P>You sure it was just a side job???  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||12
Z||000017||pred1tor83||01-06-2001||01:02 AM||||I think adding the tweeters in the back was a mistake . . . unless you are going for loudness ? ? ?  W/ the tweeters in the back and front you totally ruin your "stage" and "Imaging"   . . . but i will admit . . . it looks like a good install . . .  one question though . . . about how much space is the area between the door and the console on the 2nd fire wall ???<p>[This message has been edited by pred1tor83 (edited 01-06-2001).]||||reg||2
Z||000018||Oreif||01-06-2001||02:09 AM||||The link to the Stereo Equipment site is:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.onlinecarstereo.com/caraudio/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.onlinecarstereo.com/caraudio/</A> <BR>I usually check their monthly specials every month. (That is how I got the Polks!)<P>DAD ~ Even though it was a "side job" We have done quite a few award winning systems.<P>pred1tor83 ~ Adding tweeters to the rear is required for the surround sound processor. The processor uses 2000hz to 6000hz for it's rear output. Polk crosses the tweets at 4000hz (12db slope) Just like home theater set-up's there is a decreased level sent to the rear and it is delayed from the front, This gives you the correct staging off the front. Although the amp will drive 50W X 4, In reality I will only see maybe 10W max to the rears. The delay will be set to give the effect of the rears being farther back and wider apart to correct the imaging. The delay is variable so you can set it correctly for the type of music and the effect you want to achieve. I have heard this set-up in a Fiero and a few pick-up trucks, it sounds GREAT!<P>The space where the second firewall is, Is about 19" wide and 10" tall. The depth is about 2 1/4" deep. We installed a 10" sub in an 87GT and it "pounded" very well but we lost 3.5" of space for the seats. (Fierosound is the one who is credited with the design. His website has more details on the install.)<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||pred1tor83||01-06-2001||08:37 PM||||Kool . . . not many people do installs this complete and since you didn’t say anything about the processor I owe you an apology . . . sorry . . . ||||reg||14
Z||000020||pred1tor83||01-06-2001||08:45 PM||||i dont have a fiero (YET!!) but i was woundering would a 12" sub fit?||||reg||1
Z||000021||pred1tor83||01-06-2001||08:45 PM||||i dont have a fiero (YET!!) but i was woundering would a 12" sub fit?||||reg||1
Z||000022||Oreif||01-06-2001||09:27 PM||||A 12" will fit But you need to look at speaker depth. The cut-out of the firewall is only 2 1/4" deep so the rest needs to be added to fit the speaker. Also the volume of the box required for some 12's would be too large. ||||reg||1
Z||000023||Philphine||01-07-2001||06:53 AM||||what type of processor? will it work with a mono rear speaker? center channel output?<P>i was thinking like preditor about the tweeters but i guess with the delay and procseesing it won't matter as much.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 01-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000024||Oreif||01-07-2001||08:45 AM||||I am using an Audio Control ESP-2. If you are going to use a center channel, they make a version called an ESP-3. This provides the correct left minus right center mono channel output. <BR>||||reg||1
